			"notes": "AutoSleep 1.0.0 for Fabric 1.21.11 (client-only; servers need nothing, vanilla servers included).\n\n- Whenever the game would let you sleep (at night, or in a thunderstorm, in the Overworld), puts you in the nearest bed within 24 blocks, walking you there with the bundled Baritone if it is out of reach.\n- Follows each dimension's bed rule, so it never uses a bed that would explode:\n  - Singleplayer and LAN host: asks the game's integrated server, so datapack and modded dimensions and biomes count.\n  - On a server, in a vanilla dimension: sleeps when it is dark; never uses beds in the Nether or the End.\n  - On a server, in any other dimension: never uses a bed, because the server does not tell clients whether beds explode there.\n\nRequires Fabric API."
		}
